CONTEXT Garden IN ENGLISH
PURPOSE CONTEXT Garden
{+ The new release of the plot register of the community garden.
Plots without a keeper were overgrown last summer, so the board decided that every plot has a keeper.
This release differs from the register in use by that one rule. It starts with an empty database. +}

RELATION name[Plot*PlotName] [UNI]
MEANING "A plot has a name."
RELATION keeper[Plot*Gardener] [UNI]
MEANING "A gardener keeps a plot."
REPRESENT PlotName, Gardener TYPE ALPHANUMERIC

RULE everyPlotHasKeeper : I[Plot] |- keeper;keeper~
MEANING "Every plot has a keeper."
MESSAGE "Every plot needs a keeper."
VIOLATION (TXT "Find a keeper for ", SRC name, TXT ".")

-- The list of plots cannot be edited. A plot is edited, and a new plot is made, in a screen of its own.
-- That screen saves what the user changed as one transaction, so a new plot gets its name and its keeper together.
INTERFACE Plots : "_SESSION";V[SESSION*Plot] cRud BOX<TABLE showNavMenu>
  [ "plot" : name cRud
  , "keeper" : keeper cRud
  ]

TRANSACTIONAL INTERFACE Plot : I[Plot] CRuD BOX<FORM>
  [ "plot" : name CRUD
  , "keeper" : keeper CRUD
  ]

ENDCONTEXT
